# Test-only constructors for pinned geom2d/cross.rs and containment.rs fixtures.
import lib/bim/curve2.dl

to check cross2 {boolean:condition}:
    if condition = false:
        @intrinsic("call", "libc", "exit", nothing, 94)

to get cross2 point {a 64 bit floating-point number array of 2 items:coordinates}:
    return a cad vector2 with x (the item at 0 in coordinates) and y (the item at 1 in coordinates)

to get cross2 segment start to end:
    return the cad curve2 of (a cad line2 from (cross2 point start) to (cross2 point end))

to get cross2 circle centre with radius {a 64 bit floating-point number:radius}:
    return the cad curve2 of (a cad circle2 at (cross2 point centre) with radius radius)

to get cross2 ellipse centre with radii major and minor:
    return the cad curve2 of (the full cad ellipse arc2 on (a cad ellipse at (cross2 point centre) with radii major and minor along (cross2 point [1.0,0.0])))

to get cross2 ray origin along direction:
    return the cad curve2 of (a cad ray2 from (cross2 point origin) along (cross2 point direction))

to get cross2 xline origin along direction:
    return the cad curve2 of (a cad xline2 through (cross2 point origin) along (cross2 point direction))

to get cross2 polyline vertices with closure {boolean:closed}:
    set values to an empty list of a cad polyline vertex2
    for each row in vertices:
        set position to a cad vector2 with x (the item at 0 in row) and y (the item at 1 in row)
        append (a cad polyline vertex2 at position with bulge (the item at 2 in row)) to values
    set shape to the cad polyline2 with vertices values and closure closed
    free values
    return the cad curve2 of shape

to get cross2 interpolated spline:
    set points to a list containing (cross2 point [0.0,0.0])
    append (cross2 point [2.0,4.0]), (cross2 point [6.0,-2.0]) and (cross2 point [9.0,3.0]) to points
    set fitted to the cad nurbs2 fit through points using (the cad chord parameterization)
    free points
    check cross2 fitted's valid
    return the cad curve2 of fitted's value
